  "releaseNotes": "- (3.0.0) Removed Materializer, IMaterializer, and all related APIs,\n      including query execution, command handling, and entity materialization\n      abstractions, simplifying the library to its core high-performance\n      mapping capabilities.\n\n      - Introduced a new optimized materialization pipeline based on\n      schema-aware binding plans, hot-path caching, and expression-based\n      compiled delegates for maximum performance and predictability.\n\n      - Implemented fast-path row materializers, including fully inlined\n      expression-tree-based execution for leaf and nested entities, reducing\n      allocations, eliminating delegate indirection, and improving throughput.\n\n      - Enhanced schema matching with precomputed field snapshots and\n      flattened binding structures, replacing recursive traversal with\n      efficient linear matching strategies.\n\n      - Strengthened type validation across all mappings, ensuring provider\n      CLR type compatibility for fields and nested entities.\n\n      - Refactored internal architecture to improve separation of concerns,\n      metadata propagation, and execution clarity across mapping components.\n\n      - Expanded and consolidated unit tests to cover all materialization\n      paths, edge cases, schema variations, and concurrency scenarios,\n      ensuring high reliability.\n\n      - Improved developer tooling with an enhanced benchmark runner,\n      including interactive selection of frameworks, jobs, diagnosers,\n      and exporters.\n\n      - Updated documentation, XML comments, and README to reflect the new\n      architecture and clarified that the library has no non-Microsoft\n      dependencies.\n\n      - General code cleanup, improved exception handling, and internal\n      optimizations across the codebase.",
